    "module_designation": "Non-automatic weighing instruments",
    "description": "The UDS-series is a class III, self-indicating, non-automatic weighing instrument; the instruments are not designed for direct sales to the public. Devices: initial zero-setting device (≤20% of Max), semi-automatic zero-setting device (≤4% of Max), zero-tracking (≤4% of Max), semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing (T = -Max), zero indicator, indication of stable equilibrium device. Interfaces: serial data interface RS232C, ZigBee, Bluetooth. Legally relevant software version V 1.01, where a trailing 'x' reflects non-legally relevant changes. Sealing: access to the calibration switch is prevented by a tamper-evident lead and wire type seal. Capacity configurations are shared across types: the seven configurations (up to Max 30 kg) apply to UDS-300 and UDS-300D; the first six configurations (up to Max 15 kg) apply to UDS-600-WP and UDS-700-WP. Dual values (a/b) denote multi-interval instruments: first value applies to the lower partial range/interval, second to the upper."
